# Day 1 - Linux User Management

## Task
Create a user with a non-interactive login shell on a remote application server.

## Concepts Learned
- SSH
- Jump Host
- Application Servers
- useradd
- /usr/sbin/nologin
- sudo

## Commands Used

ssh tony@stapp01
sudo su -
useradd -s /usr/sbin/nologin john

## What I Learned

- A Jump Host acts as a gateway to remote servers.
- Every server has its own users and filesystem.
- SSH connects to a remote machine securely.
- Non-interactive users are useful for service accounts.
